From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: rockchip: rv1126: bind the RKVENC to the NPU
 thermal zone

The encoder sits in the VEPU and NPU power region, whose temperature the
NPU TSADC reports. Give the NPU thermal zone passive trips at 85 and 95
degrees Celsius like the CPU zone has, and let the encoder cool it. At
the first trip the encoder core clock and supply come down to the lowest
operating point, which are the cooling states 0 to 3, and at the second
trip the frame rate is limited as well. The zone is polled every second,
since the step_wise governor releases the cooling device on a falling
trend.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rv1126.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/rockchip/rv1126.dtsi
@@ -148,11 +148,35 @@
 		};
 
 		npu_thermal: npu-thermal {
-			polling-delay-passive = <0>;
-			polling-delay = <0>;
+			polling-delay-passive = <1000>;
+			polling-delay = <1000>;
 			thermal-sensors = <&npu_tsadc 0>;
 
+			cooling-maps {
+				map0 {
+					trip = <&npu_alert0>;
+					cooling-device = <&venc THERMAL_NO_LIMIT 3>;
+				};
+
+				map1 {
+					trip = <&npu_alert1>;
+					cooling-device = <&venc THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+				};
+			};
+
 			trips {
+				npu_alert0: npu-alert0 {
+					temperature = <85000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
+				npu_alert1: npu-alert1 {
+					temperature = <95000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
 				npu_crit: npu-crit {
 					temperature = <125000>;
 					hysteresis = <2000>;
